map of the libstdoc repository
==============================

libstdoc is a small, freestanding standard C library for Linux on
aarch64 and on x86_64.  It is built and linked without any host C
library: it provides its own program entry point, its own system-call
layer and its own formatting engine, which is what makes the test
programs a complete demonstration of the library rather than a hosted
build that happens to contain it.

The interface of the library is ISO C17: programs written in C and
programs written in C++ both link it, and the C test programs include
the internal headers as well.  The implementation behind that
interface is ISO C++23; it is compiled freestanding, so it still may
not call a host C library or use a C++ runtime.

This document lists every entry in the repository and says what it is
for.  The documents listed at the end describe the larger pieces.


