test/ - the test programs
-------------------------

    CMakeLists.txt    Builds the tests and registers them with CTest.
                      Every C test links the way a program for this
                      library would: freestanding, with the library's
                      own entry point.

    The programs:

    index.c, index.cxx
                      The original smoke test, once as C and once as
                      C++, proving the public header works from both.
                      The C++ one is a hosted program: a C++ program
                      needs the C++ runtime for its own start-up.  It
                      is compiled as C++17 on purpose, so the test
                      proves that consuming libstdoc does not require
                      C++23.
    format.c          The formatting engine, against golden output a
                      reference C library produced from the same
                      source.
    differential.c    The same engine, compiled once against the host C
                      library and once against libstdoc and compared
                      case by case, over cases built at run time.
    errors.c          The failure paths of the formatted functions.
    stream.c          The staging buffer, the discard and the order of
                      the two output streams.
    largewrite.c      One 200000 byte write through the system-call
                      layer, checked on a file and through a pipe.
    heap.c            The allocator, its safe variants and the leak
                      accounting.
    heap_abort.c      The fail-fast paths: one scenario per run,
                      selected on the command line.

    The comparison scripts:

    CompareOutput.cmake
                      Runs a program and compares its output and exit
                      status with a golden file.
    CompareMergedOutput.cmake
                      The same, with stdout and stderr merged into one
                      file first, so their order survives.
    CompareTwo.cmake  Runs two programs and requires the same bytes
                      from both.
    CheckLargeWrite.cmake
                      Runs one program twice, on a file and on a pipe,
                      and checks the status, the length and the bytes.
    CheckFatal.cmake  Requires a program to end with the documented
                      fatal status 134.
    CheckFreestanding.cmake
                      Inspects the built archive: every undefined symbol
                      has to be "main" or a libstdoc symbol, no exported
                      symbol may be a mangled C++ name, and no member
                      may hold a section that runs code before the
                      program.
    InstallTest.cmake Installs libstdoc into a scratch prefix and
                      builds consumer/ against it.
    consumer/         A small project that consumes the installed
                      package through find_package.  It is not part of
                      the libstdoc build.

    The golden files:

    expected-index.txt, expected-format.txt, expected-stream.txt
                      The output the programs are compared with.  The
                      first two were produced by a reference C library;
                      the third states a property that only libstdoc
                      defines.  See docs/testing.

    The whole directory is documented in docs/testing.


.github/ - automation
---------------------

    dependabot.yml    Keeps the GitHub Actions dependencies updated.
    workflows/aarch64-linux-gnu-ubuntu-lts-26.04.yml
                      Builds and tests the project on an aarch64
                      runner under both compilers, checks that the
                      format golden file still matches a reference C
                      library, and checks the configuration guard.
    workflows/x86_64-linux-gnu-ubuntu-lts-26.04.yml
                      The same for x86_64, with a check that the
                      architecture guard refuses an architecture that
                      is not implemented in addition.
    workflows/security.yml
                      clang-tidy, flawfinder and the dependency
                      review.
    workflows/codeql.yml
                      The CodeQL analysis workflow.  None of these
                      files takes part in the build: this repository
                      builds with no network access.


